WEBVTT

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.600
All right, my Merlin engine is
in top shape again today.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.690
Captain Charlotte Yeager!

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.730
Huh?

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.980
What the hell are you doing,
dressed like that?

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.110
Uh... I'm just testing the engine.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:51.150
That's not my point!
Uh... I'm just testing the engine.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.440
That's not my point!

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.530
Right now, we're on standby for battle.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.990
What would you do if a Neuroi showed up?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.040
But it gets so hot inside the
hangar when I rev the engine...

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.160
See! She's stripped down, too.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.500
Sheesh! You two are just terrible.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.420
Oh? So people from Karlsland are
sticklers for the rules, are they?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.170
Then what's your excuse, Hartmann?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.050
It's a billion degrees in here.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.260
H-Hartmann! You, too?

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.180
And you call yourself a Karlsland soldier?!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.520
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.710
Oh... So this is the new
model from Karlsland.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.870
More precisely, it's a prototype.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.540
Me 262 V1. It's a jet Striker.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.880
Jet?

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.340
First Lieutenant Hartmann...

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.170
Why are you dressed like that?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.640
Damn it, Hartmann!
Put some clothes on!

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.720
Huh?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.220
What's that?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.060
Apparently, a jet Striker.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.930
Jet? The thing R&D's been working on?

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.230
It arrived from Neue Karlsland this morning.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.440
It's many times more powerful than
a reciprocating engine Striker.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.490
A listed top speed of over 950 km/h.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.410
950? That's incredible!

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.620
Wow!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.330
This is the reciprocating engine
Striker's eventual replacement.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.540
Shirley, why are you dressed like that, too?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.460
What's this?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.630
Weapons specially developed for the jet Striker.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.130
One 50mm cannon.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.390
Also, four 30mm autocannons.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.060
Incredible!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.310
Can it really fly, with all that equipped?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.600
Hey, hey!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.350
Let me try this on.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.350
No. I'm gonna try it.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.940
Says who? I don't see
your name written on it!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.190
What are you talking about?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.240
If anyone should use a Striker
developed in Karlsland, it's me!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.410
Nationality has nothing to do with it.
The thing flies over 950 km/h!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.240
I'm the expert when it comes to high-speed,
so I should be the one to wear it!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.660
Is speed all you ever think about?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:32.960
Don't be such a hog.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.920
They're at it again.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.330
What to do with those two...
You're calling me a hog?!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.670
First one in!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.510
H-Hey!

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.840
No fair, Lucchini!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.840
If you wanna win, you've gotta be quick.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.230
Hmm?

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.860
Lucchini!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.160
Lucchini, what happened?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.330
I-I felt something crazy!

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.280
Something crazy?

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.370
I hate it.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.580
Shirley, don't wear it.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.880
Yeah, I think I'll pass on it.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.170
What?

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.170
Thinking about it a bit,

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.920
there's still lots I haven't done
with a reciprocating engine yet.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.300
There'll be plenty of time for jets later.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.390
Cold feet, huh?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.890
Then watch me. I'll wear it!

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.310
Incredible.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:42.820
Huh...

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:47.610
Well? With your reciprocating engine
Striker, think you can beat this?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.490
What did you say?

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:52.160
Hi, everyone! I've been looking for you.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.040
Breakfast is all ready.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:55.910
Huh?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.960
Act your age already, will you?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.840
You're behaving like a kid
who just got a new toy.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.340
Sour grapes? How pathetic.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.840
I just changed my mind.
I'm fine with this one.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.300
You Liberions love your lies of convenience.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.050
What?! You're a stubborn, military blockhead!

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.220
They're fighting again.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.190
Go!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.200
What on earth is going on?

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.660
Barkhorn-san and
Shirley-san are competing.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.950
Round one is who can go the highest!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.620
Good luck, Shirley!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:51.180
Shirley-san topped out at an
elevation of 12,000 meters.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.260
Barkhorn-san is still going. Amazing...

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.810
Huh...

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:58.980
And that's why-

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.690
Aha-ha! I win!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.360
Bitter over losing earlier?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.070
That's pathetic, Captain.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.490
Ah, it's so good!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.490
Good luck next round, Shirley.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.820
Thanks! But you know I'm gonna win.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.250
Can you fly, carrying all that?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:27.170
My P-51 is my all-purpose weapon.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.090
I know I can count on it,
no matter the situation.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.340
What's the event this time?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.510
Apparently, it's an arsenal
load competition...

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.310
To see who can carry the most weight.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:42.600
Shouldn't you start by shedding some of
that weight off your chest, Shirley-san?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.020
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.110
A-Are you okay with all that, Barkhorn-san?

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.070
This is nothing.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.910
Hey... There's no way you
can fly with all that.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.080
No way...

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.050
Target in sight.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.600
This is incredible...
This jet Striker is incredible!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.100
Holy crap.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.400
Beef stew for dinner, guys.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.610
I don't know much about cooking,

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.820
but everything you make is
always great, Miyafuji.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.740
Did you use fish stock?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.040
Yes, bonito.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.250
Thank you very much.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.420
What I want to know is why we
have to eat in this oil-soaked room.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.460
No complaints during meals.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.380
It's delicious.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:54.840
Yoshika-chan, I'm worried about
Barkhorn-san and Shirley-san.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.140
This is all I can do for them.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.680
I mean, they say people get cranky
when they're hungry, right?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.140
They do?

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:07.650
Um, aren't you tired, Barkhorn-san?

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:08.650
Yeah.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:14.360
Can you leave that there?
I need to rest a bit.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.120
Using oil drums as bathtubs...
Who'da thought, huh?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.710
Sakamoto-san said she did this
all the time when she was in Libau.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.920
Ah, Lucchini-chan! It's over capacity!

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.590
We haven't done this in forever, Yoshika!

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.930
I fill this one up all by myself.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.890
Barkhorn-san should join us...

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.190
Let her be.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:52.230
She seemed more tired than usual today.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.110
It's that thing's fault!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.320
What thing?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.530
That <i>gwaaaaaa</i> thing!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.820
You mean the jet Striker?

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:00.700
Yes, that!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.230
Ready and... go!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:29.810
Huh?

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.860
Barkhorn...

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.320
Go!

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.900
I said, "Go!"

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.710
Amazing... It's like being pushed by angels!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.260
I... I'm actually losing in a race of speed...

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.220
What just happened?

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.270
She crashed!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.160
She's awake.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:27.790
What's going on, guys?
Do I have something on my face?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.290
Barkhorn-san! I'm so glad you're okay!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.630
You crashed into the sea, Trude.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.670
What? I crashed?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:39.420
You depleted all your
magic and passed out.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.670
You don't remember?

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:44.180
That's impossible. I'd never
make such a rookie mistake.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.430
It's not your fault.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.770
Most likely, the problem
lies in the jet Striker.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.020
I can't tell for sure,

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.110
but it's possible it burns through a
considerable amount of magic.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.150
Prototypes and problems go hand in hand.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.610
But that Striker is amazing.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.870
If we want to see it in actual
combat, I must continue to test it.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.330
No.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.660
I won't let you risk more bodily injury.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:14.670
Captain Barkhorn, in addition to
being restricted from flying,

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.590
I am ordering you confined to your room.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.290
Minna!

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.340
That's an order.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.760
Understood.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.930
Use of the jet Striker is
disallowed, effective immediately.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.540
U-Um, Barkhorn-san...

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.840
What are you doing?

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.130
I'm training.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:07.510
I didn't crash because of... the jet Striker...

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.850
It was because I wasn't... strong enough...

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.270
Huh? You still plan to use it?

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:20.400
Of course. If I can master it,
I can turn the whole tide of this war.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.070
It's impossible. Give up on it.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.570
Shirley-san!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.820
Did you come to laugh at me, Liberion?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.870
Crashing because I ran out of magic...
You'd think I was a private.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.670
Listen to the Captain.
That Striker is way too dangerous.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.840
Next time, you won't just
lose the ability to fly.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:48.470
I know you understand the military
applications of the jet Striker.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.850
It's worth the risk.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.850
So you don't care if you die?

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:53.770
Huh?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:58.980
I must become stronger.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.610
You fool!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.990
Ah, a Neuroi.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.120
Hartmann-san!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.290
Were you here the whole time?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.120
Yeah.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.710
I'm going on ahead.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.920
Shirley-san, wait!

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:25.760
Yoshika-chan! We were ordered
to stay in here, on standby.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.060
An opening!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.610
You forgot something!

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.530
A transponder?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.540
It's heading due south, toward Rome.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.290
However, it's continuing to accelerate.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.790
I'm altering the rendezvous
spot. Head close to...

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.590
Unnecessary. We've got visual.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.850
It split apart?

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.930
So, it plans to overwhelm us with numbers.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.390
Five on five... Looks like
a perfect match to me.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.650
Everyone, spread out and
destroy your targets.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.110
Do not let them past us!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.400
Roger!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:27.940
Shirley.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:28.820
What is it, Major?

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:32.030
The core's inside the middle one.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.830
It's fast. I'm counting on you.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.120
Roger!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.590
There!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.680
You ain't getting away!

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:03.940
What?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:10.990
Oh, you wanna do this?

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.860
Prepare to be destroyed!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.540
Stay still!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.550
Damn it...

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.140
This is Sakamoto.
Shirley's got her hands full,

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.640
but we can't spare anyone to help.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:39.810
We need emergency backup!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.390
Roger that.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.730
Lynne-san! Miyafuji-san!

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:43.980
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.860
Barkhorn-san!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:58.240
You two will never make it in time.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.380
You're breaking a direct order, Captain!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.180
This is the only way we can save her!

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.680
But you haven't fully recovered...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.020
Trude!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.190
I'm sorry, Minna.
I'll take my punishment later.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.400
But now I must...

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:31.570
Five minutes!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.360
You have five minutes of flight!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.360
Five minutes is plenty.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.410
There!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.620
It jammed!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.250
It split again?

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.210
Crap. I'm caught in between!

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.760
Huh?

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.940
Barkhorn?!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.860
Incredible...

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:24.660
B-But use of the jet Striker was disallowed.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.410
Barkhorn... That crazy woman.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.210
Hehehe.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.420
You did it, Barkhorn!

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.670
Barkhorn, do you copy?

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.260
What's going on?
Barkhorn isn't slowing down!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.510
This is bad!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.140
The jet Striker is out of control.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.140
She's going to have all the
magic sucked right out of her!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.140
Shirley-san!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.190
On it!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:14.670
You stupid idiot!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.090
What's that sound?

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.430
Stop!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.750
Hey!

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:56.210
Those belong to me! Me!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.940
What the heck happened
while we were sleeping?

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.480
It's been torn to shreds.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.860
Sheesh. That Striker was
such a troublemaker.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.320
Yeah. And so is the person who used it.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:25.780
But thanks to her, we defeated
the Neuroi. Go easy on her.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.120
A rule is a rule!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:33.000
But it's the first time Barkhorn's
ever disobeyed an order, right?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.420
Everyone, sorry for this whole ordeal.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.340
Why are you apologizing?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.210
It's not your fault, Hartmann.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:42.260
No, I...

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:46.300
Hey, guys! Are you hungry?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:51.020
A big shipment of potatoes came in,
so we made a bunch of food.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.770
Try it, Hartmann-san.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.150
Thank you very much.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.270
Huh? Did you always wear glasses?

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:00.900
Yes, I always have.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.740
Wow, it looks delicious!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.360
Huh?

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:06.070
Oh, you try some too, Hartmann-san #2.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.030
Huh?!

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:07.870
Huh?

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.580
It's been a while, Sister.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.120
Oh, is that you, Ursula?

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.080
Sister?!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.590
This is First Lieutenant Ursula Hartmann.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.430
She's First Lieutenant Erica
Hartmann's twin sister.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.180
Twin sister?

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.140
She's one of the staff members
on the jet Striker project.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.430
Huh...

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:39.560
Captain Barkhorn, I sincerely apologize
for the trouble you experienced.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:43.690
It appears the jet Striker
possessed a fatal flaw.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:46.530
Well, prototypes and
problems go hand in hand.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:47.280
Don't worry about it.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.030
And I must apologize to you for breaking it.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.250
It's okay. All that matters
is that you're safe.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:56.620
I will take it back to Karlsland.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.080
You came all the way here to do that?

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.960
Yes. And though I doubt it makes up for it,

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.260
I brought a shipment of potatoes,
as a token of my apology.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:07.630
Th-That many again?

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.560
That's my fried potato!

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.930
Didn't you say you didn't
want any Liberion food?

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:19.900
Yes, but now I need energy to
help my body fully recover!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:22.110
Admit that they're delicious.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:23.820
They're all right.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:24.780
I said, say they're "delicious," not "all right"!

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:27.900
I made enough for everyone...
Why are they fighting over it?

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:28.950
The fact I ate it at all
should be good enough!

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:31.070
It's fine. Let them argue.

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:32.910
Leave them alone.

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:13.680
When I think about the tastiest
food in Romagna,

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:17.310
I think of rosetta, feta cheese,
supri, margherita, and acqua pazza!

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:20.310
But nothing beats my mamma's zuppa!

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:24.150
Next time on <i>Strike Witches 2:</i>
My Romagna!
